                <pb facs="0156" n="12" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg12"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">855.413 American Battle Monuments Commission/1:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Belgium</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-08-19T18:00:00-04:00">August 19, 1929—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>55. Draft enclosed with your No. 467 July 8 satisfactory to American Battle
                    Monuments Commission, who authorize General John J. Pershing, chairman of the
                    commission, who is now in Europe, to sign on behalf of the American Government.
                    Inform General Pershing and Foreign Office and arrange execution of agreement.
                    If General Pershing’s address unknown to you, inquire of Embassy at Paris.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
